.TH MAILFLAG 1 "October 2026" "MailFlag" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mailflag \- lightweight background mail and verification-code notifier
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mailflag
.RI [ OPTION ]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --settings
Open the graphical settings window. This is the default menu action.
.TP
.B --background
Run mail monitoring without opening Settings.
.TP
.B --shutdown
Ask every running MailFlag background and Settings process to exit cleanly.
This headless command is also used by Debian package removal.
.TP
.B --startup
Open the first-run wizard when no account exists; otherwise start background monitoring. Used by desktop autostart.
.TP
.B --add-account
Add a Yahoo account using the terminal fallback.
.TP
.B --remove-account [ACCOUNT]
Remove one local account, its pending state and keyring credential after confirmation. Server mail is not changed.
.TP
.B --configure-folders [ACCOUNT]
Discover and choose existing monitored IMAP folders.
.TP
.B --demo
Show an offline ordinary-mail popup demonstration.
.TP
.B --version
Show the installed MailFlag version.
.TP
.B --help
Show command help.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/mailflag/config.ini
stores non-secret settings. Credentials are stored in Secret Service.
.SH SEE ALSO
The installed README is in /usr/share/doc/mailflag/README.md.
